cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the experimental records it contains, please cite the
  software entry below. It describes the code repository only. The accompanying
  paper, "A Typed Control Contract for Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation" by
  Denys Yuvzhenko and Sergii Stirenko, has separate authorship; no DOI, venue or
  publication date is recorded here because none has been confirmed. Add a
  preferred-citation entry for the paper once those details exist.
type: software
title: >-
  typed-rag: research harness for the paper "A Typed Control Contract for Agentic
  Retrieval-Augmented Generation"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/denys-yu/typed-control-rag"
authors:
  - family-names: Yuvzhenko
    given-names: Denys
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen experimental plan, accepted semantic annotations and analysis outputs
  for a controlled comparison of four control strategies in one agentic
  retrieval-augmented generation pipeline: binary or typed context-sufficiency
  assessment, combined with an action chosen by the language model or enforced by a
  programmatic contract. The repository contains the per-run records of the main
  experiment (2,880 planned coordinates over 60 HotpotQA questions with one model)
  and a single offline command that recomputes every published estimate, table and
  figure from those records.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - agentic RAG
  - retrieval failure
  - abstention
  - HotpotQA
  - reproducibility
